               <msContents>
                  <textLang mainLang="la">Latin</textLang>
                  <msItem>
                     <title>Duns Scotus, etc.</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">MSS. 227 &amp; 228 were written in the Oxford
                        convent, but it is probable that MS. 227 at least was at York convent (q.
                        v.) at the Dissolution.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">For W. Vavaseur, Warden at Oxford c. 1500 and
                        warden of York at the dissolution see Little, Grey Friars in Oxford, p.
                        130.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="148X/149X" notBefore="1480" notAfter="1499" calendar="#gregorian">s. xv ex.</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance source="4228"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_420">Oxford, Oxfordshire. Franciscan
                        convent</orgName><p>Colophons:</p><p>1) (fol. 45v) 'Expliciunt questiones
                        doctoris subtilis super 2o. 7. 3o de anima scripte per fratrem petrum pauli
                        de Nycopia. Lord thy mercy'.</p><p>2) (fol. 119v) 'Explicit tractatus ...
                        scriptus per me fratrem Wyllelmum studentem Oxon. Anno incarnacionis
                        dominice 1419 [sic]'.</p><p>3) (fol. 215v) 'Expliciunt questiones 3i libri
                        metheorum secundum doctorem subtilem ordinis minorum ac scripte per manum
                        fratris Wyllelmum Vavysour eiusdem ordinis Anno dominice incarnacionis.
                        1491. Amen then.'</p><p> </p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Christopher Thurske' (fol.
                     218v).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Joannes Dee 1559; Novembris 24 Eboraci',
                     with ladder mark; fol. 1r.</provenance>
               <provenance cert="low" source="6343"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_610">York, Yorkshire. Franciscan
                        convent</orgName><p>MSS. 227 and 228 were written in the Oxford convent,
                        but it is probable that MS. 227 at least was at the York convent at the
                        dissolution. For the colophons in these MSS. written mainly in the Oxford
                        convent by Wm. Vavasour see under Oxford Franciscans. W. V. was warder of
                        the York Grey Friars at the dissolution and MS. 227 belonged to Christopher
                        Thurske and was acquired by John Dee at York in 1569.</p></provenance>
               </history>
